course: dictionary
lesson: 9570
title: Strangely: odd and surprising
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how something happens. «Strangely» is one of them: it tells you that something happens in an unusual or surprising way. «No birds sing, everything is strangely still.» Birds usually sing, so the silence is odd, and strangely tells you that.
explain: Use the words around strangely to check its meaning. «Crushes are normal, and they often make people act strangely: staring, blushing, showing off or going quiet.» The list after the colon shows what acting strangely looks like. Test your meaning by swapping it in: "act in an unusual way" still makes sense.
explain: Strangely can also start a sentence, where it means "surprisingly, it is odd that". «Strangely enough, the roses look brighter than ever.» Here the word does not describe how something is done. It tells you how the writer feels about the fact that follows.
explain: Strangely can also be a warning sign. If an adult is very angry, confused, or acting strangely, keep your distance and tell an adult you trust. Noticing when something is not right is a useful skill.
fact: Strangely is an adverb, so it tells you how something happens. It comes from the adjective strange, which means unusual or odd.
fact: «Strangely» means in an unusual or surprising way.
fact: At the start of a sentence, «strangely» means surprisingly, it is odd that: «Strangely enough, the roses look brighter than ever.»
fact: «Behave strangely» means act in an odd way.
fact: «Has a screw loose» is an informal phrase meaning is a bit mad or acts strangely.
exercise: «No birds sing, everything is strangely still.» What does strangely mean here? | Happily, with lots of joy | Very loudly | Slowly, like a snail | *In an unusual, surprising way
exercise: Ella says, «Pets act strangely when they are ill.» What does strangely mean in this sentence? | *In an odd, unusual way | In a quick, careful way | In a loud, noisy way | In a happy, playful way
exercise: «Strangely enough, the roses look brighter than ever.» What does strangely mean at the start of this sentence? | Slowly, one petal at a time | *Surprisingly, it is odd that | Quietly, as if no one is there
test: In «they often make people act strangely», which examples does the sentence give? | Singing and dancing at the front | Eating lunch and walking home | Reading quietly in a corner | *Staring, blushing, showing off or going quiet
test: Ben's friend is acting strangely and seems confused. What is the safe choice? | Run up and ask what is wrong | Film it to share online | Join in and copy the behaviour | *Keep your distance and tell an adult you trust
exam: What does «has a screw loose» mean? | *Is a bit mad or acts strangely | Is very tired after a long walk | Is a skilled builder | Has lost a screw from a bike
